{"record": "turn", "turn": 4, "seconds": 5.991, "response_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_details": null, "blocks": ["thinking", "tool_use"], "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 2323}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2323, "cache_read_input_tokens": 8945, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 954, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "tools": [{"id": "toolu_01KpPvg9v4qhhLjod3aRg6GD", "name": "submit_answer", "arguments": {"answer": "No. The dSph gamma-ray analysis sets a one-sided 95% CL upper limit where 2Δln L = 2.71 (ΔTS = 2.71, i.e. 1.355 in ln L), and it profiles over the per-dwarf J-factors, which carry a Gaussian prior in log10 J. The AMS-02 antiproton analysis uses ΔQ = −2Δln L = 3.84, the nominal one-parameter 95% interval threshold, and reports its upper endpoint. The paper says this differs from the common one-sided 2.71 prescription. It profiles over the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L, with a Gaussian penalty in log10 L (L̂ = 4.96 kpc, σ = 0.197, range 1–12 kpc).", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}]}, "status": "answer", "error_kind": null, "seconds": 0.0}]}
{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261125T104253Z_dev-02_staged_8160", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "No. The dSph gamma-ray analysis sets a one-sided 95% CL upper limit where 2Δln L = 2.71 (ΔTS = 2.71, i.e. 1.355 in ln L), and it profiles over the per-dwarf J-factors, which carry a Gaussian prior in log10 J. The AMS-02 antiproton analysis uses ΔQ = −2Δln L = 3.84, the nominal one-parameter 95% interval threshold, and reports its upper endpoint. The paper says this differs from the common one-sided 2.71 prescription. It profiles over the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L, with a Gaussian penalty in log10 L (L̂ = 4.96 kpc, σ = 0.197, range 1–12 kpc).", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}]}, "asked_again": null, "turns": 4, "seconds": 10.893, "tool_calls": 4, "tool_result_chars": 19594, "input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 1274, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2323, "cache_read_input_tokens": 24305, "parser_versions": ["5"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-25T10:43:04+00:00"}
